From 04939553da9a3ddb11da4db707ee48a828888c88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:06:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): fence continued operator receipts to current
 claim [daveey]

Consolidate the two receipt-continuation implementations on PR3216. Delivery
belongs to the original authenticated task/request; completion belongs to the
current admitted claim. Freeze the current run and complete request for the
transactional recheck. Carried events locate canonical Board evidence, never
authorize it. Preserve local failed/pending refusal and require proofs for
carried operator history even when the target exists locally after migration.

Preserve the original 13 historical-run cases alongside 45 completion-tool,
real pickup/remapped-ID, canonical identity and race controls. A missing ledger
alone is recoverable on the same host; the missing-request negative now removes
both carried locators too. No request rewriting, duplicate posts or DB repairs.

Proof: consolidated canonical runner 58 passed, zero failures. Previous full
Kanban run at identical production source: 877 files, 16046 passed, 24 platform
skips. Read-only replay of 22 actual databases: 354 old/new receipt evaluations,
zero as-is acceptance changes; separately labeled in-memory successor scenario
accepted 315/317 canonical-shaped historical proofs and rejected two originless
events. Nine stored claim-bearing results had zero history-gate changes. Replay
is captured-row evidence, not live canonical authentication or deployment.
